  "body": "**Swarms, Cloud, and a lighter terminal**\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Reworked swarms plan jobs in phases and parallel lanes, automatically start workers as dependencies finish, and show the whole team's progress in one pinned view\n- jcode Cloud officially launches: move a session or coordinated swarm to a VM with /cloud, keep working after disconnecting, and bring the conversation and repository back with /local\n- A lighter terminal with lower CPU usage, fewer background wakeups, faster transcript rendering, and less rendered-text memory\n\n### Improvements\n\n- In our own jcode development sessions, worker launches increased from 88 to 174 between November 2–8 and November 9–15, averaging roughly three times as many worker dispatches per active session\n- A profiled release client used 25% less CPU, idle client wakeups fell from 2.68 to 1.51 per second, and rendered-span memory in a large conversation fell from 20.4 MB to 14.6 MB\n- Spinner-frame processing became 3.5 times faster and append-frame processing on a 4,000-message transcript became 8.3 times faster\n- Cloud sessions load recent history first and fetch older messages on demand; a 7,000-message session's initial history payload shrank from 14.3 MB to 261 KB\n- Search full conversations in /resume with typo tolerance, live previews, and local and cloud sessions in the same picker\n- Set account priority tiers, hot-swap accounts with Ctrl+Alt+J/K, inspect refreshed /usage cards, and configure context limits per session\n- Follow live and completed codemode calls through bounded JavaScript previews that survive status changes and transcript compaction\n- See worker lane progress and final reports in completion messages, with clearer wait and recovery outcomes\n- Reduce polling and redraws in background windows, preserve focus state across reloads, and reuse immutable transcript and provider request data instead of repeatedly copying it\n- Live voice input includes a waveform and streaming draft transcript; model discovery and response-observed usage attribution are improved\n\n### Fixes\n\n- Recover from short network interruptions and HTTP/2 stream errors without prematurely failing the turn or suggesting an unrelated model switch\n- Improve account failover acknowledgements, retry cancellation, and protection against stale fallback resends\n- Keep the terminal in TUI mode after recovered draw panics, including tiny tmux panes\n- Improve cloud handoff recovery, repository replacement safety, reconnection, and in-place runtime reloads\n- Avoid repeated redraws for unchanged todo snapshots and repeated reads of completed background-task files\n\n**Full changelog**: https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode/compare/v0.99.1...v1.0.0\n\n<!-- jcode-platform-availability:start -->\n## Platform availability\n\n- Linux x86_64: available\n- Linux aarch64: available\n- macOS Apple Silicon: available\n- macOS Intel: available\n- Windows x86_64: available\n- Windows ARM64: available\n- FreeBSD x86_64: available\n\nWindows executables are **unsigned**. Azure Artifact Signing is not configured and the repository's existing `WINDOWS_SIGNING_REQUIRED=false` override allowed unsigned publication. Windows may show publisher or SmartScreen warnings.\n<!-- jcode-platform-availability:end -->\n\n<!-- jcode-discord-part:v1.0.0:bbfdfe46059a5cb8c8ea430b38f617191c717f1b4f8ca905f53b8b8b28b40925:1:sent:1572099390238363669 -->\n\n<!-- jcode-discord-part:v1.0.0:bbfdfe46059a5cb8c8ea430b38f617191c717f1b4f8ca905f53b8b8b28b40925:2:sent:1572099418386206731 -->\n\n<!-- jcode-discord-part:v1.0.0:bbfdfe46059a5cb8c8ea430b38f617191c717f1b4f8ca905f53b8b8b28b40925:3:sent:1572099431501668384 -->\n\n<!-- jcode-discord-part:v1.0.0:bbfdfe46059a5cb8c8ea430b38f617191c717f1b4f8ca905f53b8b8b28b40925:4:sent:1572099444730626160 -->\n\n<!-- jcode-discord-announced:v1.0.0 -->\n",
